// REJECTS: Field 'warehouse' is required
//
// A Snowflake CONNECTION spec with name, account, region and cloudType but no `warehouse`.
// This is the OTHER SnowflakeLexerGrammar -- two grammar files in two modules share that stem
// and the keyword census merges them (see ../fixtures/t2-snowflake.pure, which has to cover
// both halves in one file). ./neg-snowflake-permission-scheme.pure pins the activator half;
// this pins the connection half.
//
// snowflakeDatasourceSpecification lists sixteen elements under a `( ... )*`, all optional and
// order-free, and the walker then requires four of them -- name, account, warehouse, region --
// while leaving the other twelve genuinely optional. A rewrite reading the .g4 finds a
// sixteen-field bag with no distinguished members and accepts an unreachable warehouse.
//
// `cloudType` is supplied deliberately: it is one of the optional twelve, so its presence
// cannot be what satisfies or fails the check.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::SnowflakeNoWarehouse
{
   store: fixture::neg::Db;
   type: Snowflake;
   specification: Snowflake
   {
      name: 'test';
      account: 'account';
      region: 'us-east-1';
      cloudType: 'aws';
   };
   auth: Test;
}
